e poll is 67 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent French Hill (R) is running."]}, "overview": "French Hill, the Republican incumbent, seeks another term in a Central Arkansas district that leans about eight points Republican. Challenger Chris Jones, a Democrat, has campaigned on the economy, health care, and housing, and the two have met in several debates. Most rating outlets call the race Likely Republican, with two at Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Hill roughly an 83 percent chance of holding the seat.\n\nFundamentals put the contest closer to even: the district's Republican lean is largely offset by a national environment favoring Democrats. The most recent independent poll, from August, showed Jones narrowly ahead, but polling is sparse and dated. Hill holds a large cash advantage and outside-group support, though Jones outraised him in the third quarter. Republican complaints about Jones's financial disclosures add a late wrinkle. Hill remains favored, with modest uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2922, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2948, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2153, "margi